# Copy to .env.local. Nothing here is secret except the key.

# ── Where the text goes (§5) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The question that decides everything. Answer it before anyone puts real client
# material in the box. One module honours these: lib/ai/provider.ts
#
#   anthropic  the first-party API (default)
#   bedrock    AWS Bedrock, under the firm's existing AWS agreement
#   vertex     Google Vertex AI
#   foundry    Microsoft Foundry
VIRTUS_AI_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Required when VIRTUS_AI_PROVIDER=anthropic.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# The firm's classification line, said plainly by /api/where and in the footer
# rather than discovered during a security review.
VIRTUS_CLASSIFICATION=Internal, non-confidential or public use only. No Restricted material.

# ── Who can open it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A shared code, so a forwarded URL is not an open door. Leave it unset and
# there is no gate at all — which is what you want locally, and lesson 12.10:
# fail open on a gate that can lock you out.
#
# Not identity. It says "you were told the code" and nothing about who you are.
VIRTUS_PASSCODE=

# ── Models ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both passes default to claude-opus-5. The structure pass is a candidate for a
# cheaper model once you have measured what it costs you — that is a per-firm
# decision, which is why it is a variable and not a hardcoded downgrade.
VIRTUS_MODEL_STRUCTURE=claude-opus-5
VIRTUS_MODEL_OUTLINE=claude-opus-5

# ── Deck ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Footer on every slide.
VIRTUS_DECK_FOOTER=Internal
